From 70f89337df3b15b871fa250289d50026dc5b5a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jagpal Singh Gill <paligill@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:04:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add firmware update events to task messages

A firmware update reports its progress and failures as
xyz.openbmc_project.Software.Update events, which phosphor-logging
records as log entries. The update task reported only the activation
state, so a client watching it learnt that an update failed but not
what failed.

Watch for entries added to the logging service while a task is running
and convert the ones naming this update's software object into task
messages, so the task carries the Redfish Update registry messages for
what the update did.

Tested: In progress.

Change-Id: Iad227a099f197afdd162f99c1d002c1e5fcc4bff
Signed-off-by: Jagpal Singh Gill <paligill@gmail.com>
---
 redfish-core/lib/task.hpp           |  14 +-
 redfish-core/lib/update_service.hpp | 193 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 199 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

